WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.510
Six forty-seven p.m.

2
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.530
Claude is halfway through checkout v2…

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.150
and you have to go.

4
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.590
Next morning: two sessions, a stack of three

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.490
pull requests, and Maya waiting on a fix.

6
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:15.930
Where were you?

7
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.270
So before you leave, you type slash task.

8
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.470
Claude writes its own handoff, and parks it

9
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.410
in Baton.

10
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.730
The goal. What's done.

11
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.550
What's next. What to watch out for.

12
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.230
Every pull request it touched, with what's

13
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.930
still blocking the stack.

14
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.650
And the moment Claude needs an answer…

15
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.930
you'll know.

16
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.970
Ready to merge? Merge it right there.

17
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.470
Tomorrow, you start right where Claude left

18
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.210
off.

19
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.430
Baton. Free and open source, for Mac, Windows

20
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.650
and Linux.
